  "title": "Borrowed Current",
  "rules": [
    "The common generator sends at most one unit per turn: north, south, or alternating by clock. Its buffer holds ten.",
    "Cycle routing near [4,4]; a switch costs one buffer unit and interrupts supply on the switch turn and the following turn.",
    "Crank near [2,4] for two common units. One handcell socket trades two common units for one portable unit.",
    "Entering a gate consumes one unit from that route service capacitor. Service at the distant station consumes two from the same store.",
    "Each role must complete two private orders; a completed service flips its next target to the other station.",
    "Donate one portable unit to help a partner request. Capacitors hold four and leak one every fourth turn.",
    "A radio call publishes its stored target and tracks the sender for three turns. The old request can become stale after service.",
    "Local capacitor and agent attributes are hidden beyond radius three unless the agent is broadcasting. Gate indicators and supply pulses are public."
  ],
